\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces The digit-by-octave filing heatmap: a 9-row by 99-column grid of register bins, each cell shaded by the value of digit \ensuremath  {\times } octave mod 9, with the residue-0 bins outlined in vermillion. Computed deterministically from the digit drawers 1--9 and octave indices 1--99 --- a filing layout rather than a \texttt {textbook.models} call, though the cabinet's capacity is pinned by \breaktt {catalog\_size(octaves=99,\ precision\_digits=81)} = 8,019 in \texttt {textbook.models}. Notice the residue-0 cells recurring in a fixed diagonal pattern across the grid --- the periodic fingerprint of the mod-9 filing rule.}}{46}{figure.caption.14}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:part_0_tensor-decoupling}{{7}{46}{The digit-by-octave filing heatmap: a 9-row by 99-column grid of register bins, each cell shaded by the value of digit \texorpdfstring {\ensuremath {\times }}{x} octave mod 9, with the residue-0 bins outlined in vermillion. Computed deterministically from the digit drawers 1--9 and octave indices 1--99 --- a filing layout rather than a \protect \texttt {textbook.models} call, though the cabinet's capacity is pinned by \protect \breaktt {catalog\_size(octaves=99,\ precision\_digits=81)} = 8,019 in \protect \texttt {textbook.models}. Notice the residue-0 cells recurring in a fixed diagonal pattern across the grid --- the periodic fingerprint of the mod-9 filing rule}{figure.caption.14}{}}
