\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {24}{\ignorespaces The mass-slowing gate curve: the transduction-brake family \(v(t) = v_0\,e^{-kt}\), the book's tested model of the corpus's ``squeeze story'', plotted by \breaktt {textbook.models.transduction\_brake} for \(v_0 = 1\) with drag constants \(k = 0.5\), \(1.0\), and \(2.0\). A larger \(k\) shortens the half-life \(\ln 2 / k\), so the gate bites sooner; every curve decays toward zero without ever reaching it. The companion displacement curve stays bounded by \(v_0/k\) no matter how long the story runs.}}{109}{figure.caption.55}\protected@file@percent }
