\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {37}{\ignorespaces The densification curve \(D(x) = D_0\,(1 + k\ln (1+x))\) for the pinned parameters \(D_0 = 1\) and \(k = 1\). Plotted from \breaktt {textbook.models.densification}, with the chapter's worked checkpoints marked on the curve --- the pinned one reads \(D(4) = 1 + \ln 5 \approx 2.609438\). The takeaway mirrors the mud \ensuremath  {\to } shale \ensuremath  {\to } schist story: transformation is fast at first and slows with every further exposure, yet the accumulation never stops.}}{155}{figure.caption.89}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:part_II_metamorphic-octaves}{{37}{155}{The densification curve \(D(x) = D_0\,(1 + k\ln (1+x))\) for the pinned parameters \(D_0 = 1\) and \(k = 1\). Plotted from \protect \breaktt {textbook.models.densification}, with the chapter's worked checkpoints marked on the curve --- the pinned one reads \(D(4) = 1 + \ln 5 \approx 2.609438\). The takeaway mirrors the mud \texorpdfstring {\ensuremath {\to }}{->} shale \texorpdfstring {\ensuremath {\to }}{->} schist story: transformation is fast at first and slows with every further exposure, yet the accumulation never stops}{figure.caption.89}{}}
\newlabel{fig:part_II_metamorphic-octaves@cref}{{[figure][37][]37}{[1][155][]155}{}{}{}}
